    "submission": "submission.json",
    "summary": "Submitted an exploration that turns the last executable residual into an observed construction step.\n\nContext from the index: three findings are confirmed_in_scope, the restart check is accepted as a bounded negative, map v11 is the accepted basis, audit units are exhausted (so no new unit can be admitted), and 4 experiments remain.\n\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json with harness_heartbeat_shutdown.go, action=explore): the harness drives a single-voter in-memory node to the leader state and then calls the very handler the transport installs for heartbeats — Raft.processHeartbeat — with an identical AppendEntries request twice: once while the node is running and once after a clean Raft.Shutdown. Each call is given a buffered response channel and a 500 ms observation window, and the harness emits heartbeat_handler_response events recording responded, the response error, the elapsed time and the node state, so the running call (which reaches appendEntries and answers through rpc.Respond) can be compared directly with the shutdown call.\n\nThis is deliberately an exploration, not a check: unit admission is exhausted and exploration output guides construction without adding property Evidence, so the residual that the map names on b-follower-append (the shutdown branch of processHeartbeat dropping the request while a transport consumer waits for a response) is either observed as a difference or bounded as not reached, and any later requirement would need its own accepted unit, fresh execution and correspondence review.\n\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and the clean-copy execution remain with the controller."
